{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>קול</b> — He mentions YHWH, because His power and might are seen at the time the rain comes down, as written in Job: \"Who does great things beyond search,\" and after it: \"Who gives rain.\" And because he mentioned the glory of His name, he called the thunder כבוד, and this is the meaning of קול ה' על המים." "And the meaning of ה' על מים רבים — that He brings thunder. And note, the word הרעים draws itself along and another [word] with it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:50.855463915Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}